  "result": "Perfect! I've successfully implemented the payments module. Here's a summary of what was created:\n\n## Implementation Summary\n\n**Created `src/payments.js`** with three functions:\n\n1. **`recordPayment(invoice, { amount, date })`** \u2014 Records a payment on an issued or partially paid invoice\n   - Validates invoice status is 'issued' or 'partially_paid' (returns NOT_ISSUED error otherwise)\n   - Validates amount is a positive integer in cents (returns AMOUNT_INVALID error otherwise)\n   - Checks payment doesn't exceed what's owed (returns OVERPAYMENT error if it does)\n   - Adds payment to `invoice.payments` array (creates it if missing)\n   - Updates status to 'paid' when balance reaches 0, or 'partially_paid' while owing remains\n   - Returns `ok(newInvoice)` with payment added\n\n2. **`balanceDue(invoice)`** \u2014 Returns the total amount still owed (invoice total minus payments)\n\n3. **`totalPaid(invoice)`** \u2014 Helper that sums all payments made\n\n**Updated `src/errors.js`** with two new error codes:\n- `NOT_ISSUED`: \"Invoice must be issued or partially paid before recording a payment.\"\n- `OVERPAYMENT`: \"Payment exceeds the amount still owed.\"\n\n**Added comprehensive tests** in `test/payments.test.js` with 27 test cases covering:\n- Balance and payment calculations\n- Status transitions (issued \u2192 partially_paid \u2192 paid)\n- Error validation (invalid amounts, overpayments, wrong status)\n- Data immutability and preservation\n- Payment history tracking\n- Edge cases (1 cent payments, exact balance payments)\n\nAll 158 tests pass (27 new + 131 existing).",
